{
  "duration": 64.48,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 8.28,
      "text": " Jupiter fills the sky, not a postcard, a giant, storm bans rolling like weather on a world"
    },
    {
      "start": 8.28,
      "end": 16.66,
      "text": " that could swallow a thousand earths, and beside it, small, bright, cracked white Europa."
    },
    {
      "start": 17.96,
      "end": 26.72,
      "text": " Orbit drifts closer, cream eyes wide. The ice is not smooth, it is scarred, a frozen ocean"
    },
    {
      "start": 26.72,
      "end": 33.58,
      "text": " shell, cut with long, dark lines like something moved underneath and left fingerprints in the"
    },
    {
      "start": 33.58,
      "end": 40.4,
      "text": " cold. What if the most important ocean in our solar system is the one we cannot see,"
    },
    {
      "start": 41.24,
      "end": 51.88,
      "text": " not on the surface, under the ice, dark, pressed, liquid. Orbit tips toward the cracks, antenna"
    },
    {
      "start": 51.88,
      "end": 58.66,
      "text": " glowing. The journey is not past this moon, the journey is through it, into whatever"
    },
    {
      "start": 58.66,
      "end": 64.28,
      "text": " weights below the frozen lid. Could life exist under the ice of Europa?"
    }
  ],
